{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Remove the Primary Earner Income Cap on the Marriage Allowance",
        "additional_details": "This cut-off seems to unfairly arbitrary & penalises single-earner households. A family where one parent earns \u00a355,000 receives zero benefit from the unused personal allowance of the stay-at-home parent. In stark contrast, a dual-income household earning \u00a350,000 across two jobs benefits from two full personal allowances, totalling \u00a325,140 tax-free. This creates a severe tax penalty for families shouldering the burden of single-handedly providing for their household in a punishing economy which removing the Primary Earner Income Cap would go some way to mitigate.",
        "background": "The combination of rising living & childcare costs can force families onto one income. The \u00a350,270 Cap stops single earners from receiving the \u00a31,260 Marriage Allowance transfer. If removed this would provide vital \u00a3252 tax relief, ending what we feel is an unfair penalty on single-earner households",
